@startuml sequence-oai-pmh-harvest
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: an incremental harvest is a keyset walk over oai_records ordered by
'       (datestamp, id) between from and until; the until bound is frozen into
'       a signed, stateless resumption token so every page of one list sees the
'       same range, and the final page carries an empty token.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, proposal (IP-033). Scope: one ListRecords list
'       of 150 records in pages of 100 plus the error branches. Omitted:
'       GetRecord, ListSets, Identify (same path, single response).
' Source: OAI-PMH 2.0 spec §2.5, §2.7.1, §3.3, §3.5, §3.6, §4.1-§4.2 (read
'         verbatim), §4.3-§4.6 (read as a summary) and guidelines-repository
'         §3, §5 (openarchives.org, read 2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Incremental ListRecords: keyset pages, frozen until, empty final token (proposal IP-033, 2026-11-16)

actor "Harvester" as harvester
participant "OaiPmhView\n/oai" as view
participant "RequestParser" as parser
participant "OaiRepository" as repo
participant "TokenCodec" as tokens
database "oai_records" as records
participant "Crosswalk\nmarc21" as crosswalk

== first page ==
harvester -[$accent_msg()]> view : <b>GET ?verb=ListRecords&metadataPrefix=marc21</b>\n<b>&from=2026-11-15T00:00:00Z&set=stu</b>
view -> parser : parse(GET or POST form)
parser --> view : OaiRequest (or badVerb · badArgument:\nrepeated key, from > until, mixed granularity)
view -> repo : handle(request)
repo -> repo : responseDate = now (whole seconds, UTC)\nuntil = until or responseDate
repo -> records : count(set, from..until) → 150\nSELECT … ORDER BY datestamp, id LIMIT 101
records --> repo : 101 rows (live + tombstones)
loop first 100 rows
  alt deleted
    repo -> repo : header status="deleted", no metadata
  else live
    repo -> crosswalk : render(projection)
    crosswalk --> repo : <record> MARC21 slim
  end
end
repo -> tokens : encode(prefix, set, from, until,\nafter = (ds, id) of row 100, cursor 100)
tokens --> repo : signed token
repo --> view : records + <resumptionToken\ncompleteListSize="150" cursor="0">
view --> harvester : 200 text/xml; charset=utf-8

== next page ==
harvester -[$accent_msg()]> view : <b>GET ?verb=ListRecords&resumptionToken=…</b>
view -> tokens : decode(token)
alt bad signature or other argument
  view --> harvester : 200 error badResumptionToken · badArgument
else valid
  view -> repo : handle(request from token)
  repo -> records : WHERE (datestamp, id) > after\nAND same set, from..until LIMIT 101
  records --> repo : 50 rows
  repo --> view : 50 records + empty <resumptionToken cursor="100"/>
  view --> harvester : 200 text/xml (list complete)
end

== error branches (no list) ==
harvester -> view : metadataPrefix=mods
view --> harvester : error cannotDisseminateFormat
harvester -> view : from=2026-12-01 (nothing changed since)
view --> harvester : error noRecordsMatch
harvester -> view : set=unknown
view --> harvester : error noRecordsMatch (set exists in ListSets\nor not: the empty list is the answer)

caption The token carries every argument plus the last (datestamp, id), signed with the Django secret: no server state, any worker can serve the\nnext page, and the same token re-issued returns the same page. A record changed during the walk gets a newer datestamp, so it\nleaves the frozen range and comes with the next harvest (§5, allowed). The harvester reuses responseDate as its next from.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/sequence-oai-pmh-harvest.puml
@enduml
